    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Steps to reproduce\n\n`init.lua`:\n```lua\nlocal buffer = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(false, false)\nvim.api.nvim_open_tabpage(buffer, true, { after = 0 })\n```\nWith just the config above, running `nvim some_file` will cause two tabs to open.\nThe first is empty as expected.\nThe second is `some_file`, but weirdly it doesn't show the file's contents and is instead empty.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.4\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux Mint 22.1 Cinnamon 6.4.8",
